        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="flow-stage">
        <span class="stage-number" aria-hidden="true">
          03
        </span>
        <h3>Serve</h3>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
          ↓
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-content">
        <p class="stage-intro">
          Prepared Parquet data can be queried through a SQL layer.
        </p>
        <table>
          <caption>Fictional summary · one row per activity</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Activity</th>
              <th scope="col">Items</th>
              <th scope="col">Units</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Sketch</td>
              <td>2</td>
              <td>5</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="flow-stage">
        <span class="stage-number" aria-hidden="true">
          04
        </span>
        <h3>Apply</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-content">
        <p class="stage-intro">
          A report or notebook reads the same prepared summary.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Sketch accounts for 5 known units.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="quality-note">
          Review cannot be quantified until its missing value is resolved. A
